<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Mainland Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Khmer Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1970 CE – 1975 CE · capital Phnom Penh</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The US-backed Cambodian republic of Lon Nol, which deposed Sihanouk in 1970 and fell to the Khmer Rouge in April 1975.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>On 18 March 1970 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodia">Cambodia's</a> national assembly, led by Prime Minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lon-nol">Lon Nol</a> and Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sisowath-sirik-matak">Sisowath Sirik Matak</a>, voted to remove <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norodom-sihanouk">Norodom Sihanouk</a> as head of state while he was abroad. The monarchy was abolished and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-empire">Khmer</a> Republic proclaimed on 9 October 1970.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lon-nol">Lon Nol</a>, who became president in 1972, sought to expel North Vietnamese forces from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-cambodia-1953-1970">Cambodia</a> and received US military aid. The republic was weakened by corruption, an inexperienced army and Lon Nol's ill health. US bombing of the countryside intensified, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-rouge">Khmer Rouge</a>, now allied with the exiled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norodom-sihanouk">Sihanouk</a>, gained recruits. Refugees swelled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phnom-penh">Phnom Penh</a> to over two million.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-rouge">Khmer Rouge</a> forces besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phnom-penh">Phnom Penh</a> in early 1975. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lon-nol">Lon Nol</a> fled on 1 April, the US evacuated its embassy, and on 17 April 1975 the city fell. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-empire">Khmer</a> Rouge emptied the capital and established <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/democratic-kampuchea">Democratic Kampuchea</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/khmer-republic.jpg" alt="Khmer Republic" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Himasaram · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Khmer_Republic.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1970 CE – 1975 CE</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Phnom Penh</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Lon Nol, Cheng Heng</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Theravada Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Khmer</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Cambodia</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>République khmère</dd></dl></aside></div>
